{"name":"Earthling","hex":"#ded6c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Earthling","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inhabitant of Earth, as opposed to one of heaven. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An inhabitant of Earth, as opposed to one of another planet; specifically, a sentient member of any species native to Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Earthling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Earthling (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Earthling is a 2010 sci-fi film by Clay Liford starring Rebecca Spence, Peter Greene and William Katt."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/Earthling2010filmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthling_(film)"},{"title":"Earthlings (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Earthlings is a 2005 American documentary film about humanity's use of non-human animals as pets, food, clothing, entertainment, and for scientific research. The film is narrated by Joaquin Phoenix, features music by Moby, and was directed by Shaun Monson, executive produced by Libra Max and co-produced by Maggie Q. A sequel titled Unity was released in 2015."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Earthlings_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthlings_(film)"},{"title":"Earthling (David Bowie album)","blocks":[{"text":"Earthling is the twenty-first studio album by the English musician David Bowie, released on 3 February 1997 through RCA Records in the United Kingdom, Virgin Records in the United States, and Arista Records/BMG in other territories. Mostly self-produced by Bowie, it was primarily recorded from August to October 1996 at New York City's Looking Glass Studios. Bowie composed the tracks with Reeves Gabrels and Mark Plati, who are credited as co-producers, with Mike Garson, Gail Ann Dorsey and Zack Alford providing overdubs later."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Earthling_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthling_(David_Bowie_album)"},{"title":"Earthling (Eddie Vedder album)","blocks":[{"text":"Earthling is the third solo studio album by American singer-songwriter Eddie Vedder. The album was released on February 11, 2022, by Republic Records and Seattle Surf."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/Eddie_Vedder_Earthling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthling_(Eddie_Vedder_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg/500px-150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg/1280px-150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg/500px-150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_%287815846936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guitarist Reeves Gabrels (pictured in 2012) was one of Bowie's primary collaborators for Earthling.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A150-minute_almost_non-stop_show_not_enough_for_The_Cure_at_Frequency_Festival_(7815846936).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Neil_Young_1996.jpg/500px-Neil_Young_1996.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Neil_Young_1996.jpg/500px-Neil_Young_1996.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Neil Young (pictured in 1996) influenced the lyrics of \"Dead Man Walking\" after Bowie performed at a pair of benefit concerts for the artist in October 1996.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANeil_Young_1996.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg/500px-Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg/1280px-Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg/500px-Coat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Union Jack coat on display at the David Bowie Is exhibition in 2018.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoat_designed_by_Alexander_McQueen_for_David_Bowie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/David_Bowie_1997.jpg/500px-David_Bowie_1997.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/David_Bowie_1997.jpg/1280px-David_Bowie_1997.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Da